    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d562">

                <pb facs="0796" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.71247H/70: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Sydney</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Preston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sydney</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-12-03T17:00:00+10:00">December 3, 1936—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 3—9:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of October 23, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d562-f1"/>
                    enabling legislation introduced in Parliament today to exclude American vessels
                    from Tasman trade. Bill based on similar New Zealand legislation. Probably no
                    final action until after Christmas recess and indications are it will pass by
                    substantial majority. I will send copy of bill as soon as received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Preston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
